     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Pronunciation",
     "title": "HALF without l, a-STERN",
     "paras": [
      "<b>half</b> /hɑːf/: the <i>l</i> is silent, like <i>calf</i>. Not <i>halv</i>, not <i>hal-f</i>.",
      "<b>astern</b> /əˈstɜːn/: the strong part is <b>STERN</b>, and the <i>a</i> is very short: <i>uh-STERN</i>.",
      "Orders are said with two strong words: <b>DEAD SLOW a-HEAD</b>. <b>HALF a-STERN</b>."
